'''Gossams''' were a diminutive [[Color|blue]]-skinned [[species]] native to the [[planet]] [[Castell]] located in the [[Colonies]] region of [[the galaxy]]. Several Gossams, such as [[Shu Mai]] and [[Amita Fonti]], allied themselves with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]].

==Biology and appearance==
Gossams were a [[Reptile|saurian]]<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]<ref name="Attack of the Clones" /> hailing from the [[planet]] [[Castell]].<ref name="Geektionary" /> They were a squat people with wrinkled<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> blue skin and long necks<ref name="Attack of the Clones" /> sometimes covered with neck rings. They had three-toed feet.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

==Society and culture==
Gossams such as [[Shu Mai]] were obsessed with status, power, and wealth. She wore jewellery including neck rings, an emblazoned jewel crest, and a rich skirt made of rare [[uris silk]].<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

==History==
Gossam Shu Mai served as [[Presidente]] of the [[Commerce Guild]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> using aggressive tactics to work her way up the company to outdo rivals for leadership.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> She controlled the pooled financial resources of some of the galaxy's largest corporations, and covertly lent her Guild's support to the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> [[Cat Miin]] served as her aide,<ref name="Complete Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> while fellow Gossam [[Amita Fonti]] sat on the [[Separatist Senate]].<ref name="Heroes on Both Sides">{{TCW|Heroes on Both Sides}}</ref> The [[Gossam Commandos]] of the [[Commerce Guild Punitive Security Forces]] became part of the [[Confederacy military]].<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref>

